m-weight perfect matching on its odd-degree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumWeightMatching"},{"type":"text","text":"), and an Eulerian circuit of their union by Hierholzer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the first vertex, shortcut to the first visit of each vertex. The matching is on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complete graph of the odd vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order (pairs i < j lexicographic), and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"circuit’s multigraph lists the tree edges by position, then the matched pairs in that order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the tour is determined. At most 3\/2 × the shortest tour when the weights satisfy the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"triangle inequality (not checked)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tours read the simple graph, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" documents; nil below three"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is complete; the sum along a tour fits in "},{"code":"W","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". When "},{"code":"W","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"FixedWidthInteger","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", every non-loop edge’s weight satisfies n · (2 · |weight| + 1) ≤"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"W.max \/ 8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the matching’s bound), checked as each weight is read, so a weight beyond it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps even on an edge the matching never sees; so n ≤ "},{"code":"W.max \/ 8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (15 vertices for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Int8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), whatever the weights. An arbitrary-precision integer has no bound."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n³): the matching on up to n vertices; the tree O(n²)."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Christofides’ tour (Christofides 1976; Serdyukov 1978).","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/christofidestour(weight:)-6qvc8"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/christofidesTour(weight:)-6qvc8","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","title":"Vertex"},"doc://Walks/documentation/Walks/Cycle":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cycle","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":